NAME
       tty - print the name of the terminal you are typing in

SYNOPSIS
       tty

DESCRIPTION
       tty prints the device of the terminal connected to standard input,
       such as /dev/tty1 for the first text console or /dev/pts/0 for an ssh
       or terminal-window session. It prints "not a tty" (and exits with 1)
       when standard input is not a terminal, for example in a script run by
       cron. The names match the TTY column of who, w and ps.

EXAMPLES
           tty

SEE ALSO
       who(1), w(1), ps(1)
